const DSL_REF = `Binokor command language (one command per line; '#' starts a comment; units: metres with '.' decimal; plan y axis points DOWN/south, x east).
Points: grid node like А1 (row letter + column number; Cyrillic letters А Б В Г Д Е Ж И К Л М Н П Р С Т), node with offset А1+0.5,0, absolute 3.6,6.0, relative to previous point @1.2,0.
grid x 3.6 3.3 3.6 (column spacings → axes 1,2,3,4) | grid y 6 1.8 6 (row spacings → axes А,Б,В,Г) | grid add NAME POINT ANGLE_DEG | grid polar PREFIX CENTER n=12 step=30 [a0=0] (radial axes PREFIX1…n as rays from the centre; angles in plan coordinates) | grid circ NAME CENTER RADIUS (circular axis) | grid move NAME dx,dy | grid del NAME
Curved walls: a circle = two arc walls (wall T a b arc=top; wall T b a arc=bottom); an oval/ellipse = 4–8 arc walls; windows and doors may be placed on arc walls (s = distance along the arc), each opening becomes a flat chord.
Editing: dup ID[,ID] dx,dy n=6 (array of copies) | extend ID[.a|.b] TARGET (wall/beam/grid line) | join ID1 ID2 (corner) | trim ID x,y (remove the piece between neighbouring wall crossings at that point) | lock / unlock ID[,ID]
levels N H [first H1] (resets levels L1..LN) | level add [H] | level below [H] (basement) | level h L2 3.3 | level name L1 Text | project Name
wall TYPE P1 P2 [P3 ...] [ref=l|c|r] [h=2.4] [arc=MIDPOINT] LEVEL   (types: T400 exterior 400mm, M200 bearing concrete 200, P120 partition 120; a chain of points makes several walls; ref=r puts the body on the right of the drawing direction; LEVEL is L1, L2… or all)
column [C400|C300|C500x300] POINT [rot=deg] LEVEL | beam [B300x500|B400x600|B250x400] P1 P2 LEVEL
window TYPE WALLID OFFSET (offset in m from the wall's start point to the window centre; types O15 1500×1500, O21 2100×1500, O09 900×1500) | window TYPE NODE1 NODE2 LEVEL (centred between two nodes on a wall)
door TYPE WALLID OFFSET | door TYPE NODE1 NODE2 LEVEL (types D10 1000, D08 800, D07 700)
stair P1 P2 LEVEL (rectangle; needs ≈4.8×2.3 m for a 3 m storey) | zone POINT Name_With_Underscores LEVEL | slab P1 P2 P3 … [t=0.2] LEVEL | hole SLABID P1 P2 P3 …
foundation strip [w=0.6 d=1.5] | footing POINT [b=1.5 d=1.5] | roof flat|gable|hip [SLOPE_DEG] [over=0.5] | section NAME P1 P2 | dim P1 P2 [off=0.8] LEVEL | text POINT Words_With_Underscores LEVEL
walltype NAME bearing|partition Material:mm:lambda … | wintype NAME width_mm height_mm [sill=0.85] | doortype NAME width_mm height_mm (custom types, put them before use)
lenta POINT [rot=deg] [key=value …] — exhibition «ribbon»: wavy superellipse plan L×W (n, wv), recessed glazed ground floor (gH, sb = cantilever), perforated green ceramic cladding (pw×phh panels, hole share) with a wavy top edge (Ha, nw, ph) leaning out (lean), roof terrace at Hb, external spiral ramp to the roof (rw, rs %, ru start), floors fh, atrium atr, cores, evac.
site lat=… lon=… [elev=m] [addr=…] [town=…] [region=…] [country=…] [epsg=32642] [e= n=] [rot=deg] — site location: IfcSite lat/lon/elevation, IfcPostalAddress, IfcMapConversion to UTM (E/N computed from lat/lon unless given); also the default latitude for insolation
seksiya POINT [rot=deg] [key=value …] — residential sections with apartment-mix rules: nS sections of nM facade modules (mod) in a row, depth D (≥ dC → double-loaded middle corridor with through end apartments; < dC → single-loaded corridor along the north-most facade with corner end apartments); core = stair(s) | lift lobby to the facade | lifts; apartments S/M/L (sz) mixed by m1…m4 %, rooms ≤ rD deep with hall + wet rooms on the corridor side; ground floor gf (0 flats + through hall, 1 retail); exterior wall build-up mat (0 aerated block, 1 RC + ventilated facade, 2 sandwich panel, 3 brick cavity) with R/U; checks: 2 stairs above fA m², corridor ≥ 1.2, lobby ≥ 1.6, smoke-free stair above h28, ≤ aMax flats per core, north-only flats, insolated rooms, minimum room/apartment areas (all norms are parameters). IFC: storey per floor, IfcSpace per room with Qto/Pset, IfcZone per apartment, material layer sets, wall/slab/door/window types, windows and doors in openings
pixel POINT [rot=deg] [key=value …] — stepped «pixel» housing: N blocks of bw×D along the length, shifted sh across (zz=1 zig-zag, 0 one-way steps), floors nHi→nLo (lower roofs become terraces with planters), double-loaded corridor cw with apartments aw wide on both sides, cores every coreE blocks (evac check), projecting white balcony boxes (share bx, bxW×bxD, plant share with planters), glazed retail ground floor gH set back sbG under a curved canopy slab (ov), basement parking pk levels extended pkX with ramp rs % and demand pkR per apartment (stall m² per space); flags single-aspect north apartments.
oval POINT [rot=deg] [key=value …] — an oval hall: superellipse plan A×B (ne exponent), pillow section (H, bulge, rtop), triangulated lattice facade (cell, solid share of white panels, w depth, tw thickness), glass gl behind; entrance arches where the facade edge lifts (arches 0-2, archA direction deg, archH, archW half-width, archD glass recess), floors (fh, clr, void atrium share, cores, evac), striped plaza in front (plazaW, plazaD, stripe). Change with set V1 key=value.
stadium POINT [rot=deg] [key=value …] — a stadium: pitch pL×pW with run-off, seating bowl whose row risers follow the sightline C-value (c, eye, tread, rows, wall0), a torus roof of wavy timber lamellas (R, ri inner roof edge over the pitch, H, crown, bulge, n, f, amp, w, tw, gl), concourse floors under the stands (fh, clr, cores, conc), egress parameters (vom spacing, vomW, flow persons/m/min, tEv minutes, row seats to an aisle), site: platform over water (plat), radial bridges (arms, armA, armW, armL), planted islands (isl). Change with set R1 key=value.
bar POINT [rot=deg, default 90] [key=value …] — a layered residential slab block (Zaha Hadid CityLife-like): L W (axis length, depth m), bp bend (bend position 0..1, bend angle deg), nLo nHi (storeys of the low wing / tall end), sw0 sw1 (where the roof rises, 0..1), tip (extra prow height m), h (storey height), rc (plan corner radius), bal balL balK (balcony max projection m, wave length m, phase shift per storey), wood white woodL woodK para (facade pattern: wood share, white share, pattern length, diagonal shift, solid parapet share), cor (corridor width), evac (max distance door→stair m), minw (min room width), mix1 mix2 mix3 (apartment mix %), seed. Interior (corridor, stair-lift cores on the worse-oriented side, apartments with rooms) is generated. Change with set U1 key=value.
shell POINT [rot=deg] [key=value …] — a parametric free-form shell (lofted cross-sections along x): L W (length, depth m), h0 (base height), p1h p1c p1s / p2h p2c p2s / p3h p3c p3s (roof peaks: extra height, position 0..1 along length, width), e1h e1c e1w / e2h e2c e2w / e3h e3c e3w (front edge lifts = openings: height, position, width), eb (back edge lift), top (crest position across, 0 front..1 back), curl (how far the lifted rim cantilevers out and folds under itself, m), lip (rim radius), land (length of the ramp where the skin meets the ground tangentially), tail (left tail rise length 0..0.4), soft (smoothing of arch legs, m), tw twc (roll of the ribbon around its own axis at the right end, degrees, and where it starts 0..1), rib ribn (stepped pillow ribs on the left peak: depth m, count), fh clr room cor core evac fire (interior floors: storey height m (0 = none), minimum headroom m, room module along the length m, corridor width m, max spacing of stair-lift cores m, allowed travel distance to a stair m, max fire compartment area m²), wn (end narrowing), t (thickness), setb (glazing set back behind the rim), nu nv (mesh). Change with set Q1 key=value.
form POINT [rot=deg] [key=value …] — a floor-by-floor free-form tower mass (two towers merging into a terraced base); keys: n1 n2 (storeys of left/right tower), h (storey height), rb (base radius), rt1 rt2 (top radii), sep (half distance between tower centres at top), d0 (same at bottom), split merge (0..1 height fractions where the towers separate), flare (base flare 0..1), k0 kmin (blend radius bottom/top, m), pod (terraced podium storeys), terr (terrace depth), fin fd fw (vertical fin spacing, depth, thickness, m), crown (top setback steps), seg (contour segments), ell (base elongation), lean (towers lean, m). Change with set K1 key=value.
copy L1 all|L2 (copies walls, columns, openings to other levels) | move ID[,ID] dx,dy | dup ID[,ID] dx,dy [LEVEL] | rotate ID[,ID] cx,cy deg | mirror ID[,ID] P1 P2 | set ID key=value (type, ref, h, s, rot, name, t) | delete ID[,ID]
New element IDs are prefix + a global counter: W walls, C columns, O windows, D doors, S stairs, Z zones, P slabs, B beams, F footings — the next free number is given below.
Rules: openings must stay ≥ 0.15 m away from any grid axis crossing their wall and inside the wall; keep 0.3 m between openings; bearing walls of upper storeys must stand on bearing walls or columns below.`;
